{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "2c2160d735514c42ac7c3d63a8e1711a", "pid": 15226, "time": "2026-10-10T11:04:11-0700", "elapsed_s": 176.681, "artifact": "out/det-ab-2.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["date_of_birth", "phone_last4"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "robot", "refuse_to_talk", "cannot_answer", "change_recorded_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "missing_date_parts", "text": "The documents do not say how to interpret a promise date given without a month or year (e.g. 'the 15th').", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "hardship_multi_product", "text": "Brief B rule 9 continues the call only for dispute and already-paid claims; it does not say whether a declined hardship transfer ends the call or is noted per product and the call continues. Kept Brief A rule 32 (close as no_promise / hardship).", "doc": "sources/001-brief-b.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.opening: removed the added 'Hello,'. The brief only dictates the content (digital assistant, Freya Bank, call recorded), so the sentence now says only that; opening_verbatim stays false.", "special_cases[already_paid].source and special_cases[dispute].source: now quote Brief A rules 39/40 along with Brief B rule 9 (the override), so the sources show where the sentence and the trigger come from.", "Expanded source spans for identity (rule 15 decline), third_party (rule 8 wrong number), amounts (rules 24, 27), outcomes (transfer-after-promise and goodbye), multi_product (rules 6 and 10), phrases (holder question, Brief B all-today question) and promise_write (rules 34 and 36) to cover every value they back. No values changed."], "audit_unresolved": ["How to read a promise date given without a month or year (e.g. 'the 15th'): not stated; calendar.missing_date_parts left as 'unresolved'.", "Multi-product hardship: Brief B rule 9 continues the call only for dispute and already-paid claims. It does not say whether a declined hardship offer ends the call or is noted per product while the call continues. Brief A rule 32 (close no_promise/hardship) is kept.", "Sympathy sentence for hardship: the brief only asks for 'one short sentence of sympathy'. 'I am sorry to hear that.' is a written sentence, not words the brief dictates."]}
